                        <surname>Nicholson</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1765">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1844"/>
                    <occupation>Architect and mathematician</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Godwin sees P Nicholson between 1819 and 1820, and then again in 1826 and
                            1829. Peter Nicholson hasd by then returned to London where he was
                            engaged in a range of publishing endeaours. Godwin's association with
                            him might well be related to his connections with Nash and Soane at this
                            time (esp 1820) when he is looking for someone to take William junr on
                            as an apprentice. Indeed, he does then take William with him on one occasion in 1820 after an exchange of letters.</p>
                        <p>The 1804 Nicholson (P H) is not connected - it is not Godwin's practice
                            to add initials in brackets and PH probably rfers to the topic of his
                            writing to William Nicholson.</p>
                    </note>
